1
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:04,870
Oh, Phoebe, are you still on hold?

2
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:07,420
I was supposed to call my dad back, like, two hours ago.

3
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:09,090
Oh, yeah. He clicked on.

4
00:00:09,250 --> 00:00:11,210
He said call him as soon as you get a chance.

5
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:13,760
- He's at Flimbees.     - What's Flimbees?

6
00:00:13,930 --> 00:00:16,970
Oh, yeah, that's the word I use when I can't remember the real thing.

7
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,970
Okay, hang up. That's it. Come on.

8
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:23,390
No. Rachel, that's what they want me to do.

9
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:26,230
My warranty expires tomorrow. If I don't get through...

10
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:29,110
...they're not gonna fix my crappy, broken phone for free.

11
00:00:29,270 --> 00:00:31,440
We cannot let them win. It's us versus them.

12
00:00:31,610 --> 00:00:33,110
Yes.

13
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:36,570
- Hey.     - Hi.

14
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:39,580
Uh, listen, I gotta double-check for tickets tonight. Who got what?

15
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:41,240
- I have one.   - I have one.

16
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:43,950
I need two. I'm bringing Pete.

17
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:45,460
My boyfriend.

18
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:49,590
I have a boyfriend now.

19
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:51,550
Two it is. Ross, how about you?

20
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:54,840
Uh, yeah, I, uh... I also need two.

21
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:57,550
Really? Who's number two?

22
00:00:57,720 --> 00:00:59,010
Whose Number Two?

23
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:02,220
One of the more difficult games sewer workers play.

24
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:06,270
Uh, no one, it's just this person.

25
00:01:06,770 --> 00:01:08,400
Like a date-type person?

26
00:01:08,770 --> 00:01:11,520
Yeah, kind of. Uh, it's this woman from work.

27
00:01:11,690 --> 00:01:14,940
I hope that won't be too weird. Will it, Rach?

28
00:01:15,110 --> 00:01:18,910
No. No, not at all. I was actually gonna bring someone myself so...

29
00:01:19,450 --> 00:01:21,870
But you said one ticket.

30
00:01:24,790 --> 00:01:27,120
I meant me plus one.

31
00:01:27,790 --> 00:01:30,290
Okay. Did, uh, you guys mean you plus one?

32
00:01:32,630 --> 00:01:34,420
- All right. I'll see you tonight.     - Okay.

33
00:01:34,590 --> 00:01:35,880
- Okay. Bye-bye.     - Bye.

34
00:01:36,050 --> 00:01:37,300
Bye-bye.

35
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:38,880
Okay, I need a date.

36
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:44,350
Oh, hey. You guys are finally gonna get to meet Kate.

37
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:47,100
And I, uh, borrowed some of your cologne. I hope she likes it.

38
00:01:47,270 --> 00:01:49,060
What are you doing? That's never gonna happen.

39
00:01:49,230 --> 00:01:52,560
- She's seeing somebody.     - Yeah. And I don't have any cologne.

40
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:56,940
- Green bottle next to the shaving cream.     - Oh. Worm medicine for the duck.

41
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,500
# So no one told you life was gonna be this way #

42
00:02:09,070 --> 00:02:13,240
# Your job's a joke, you're broke, your love life's D.O.A. #

43
00:02:14,150 --> 00:02:17,960
# It's like you're always stuck in second gear #

44
00:02:18,420 --> 00:02:20,520
# When it hasn't been your day, #

45
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:23,520
# your week, your month, or even your year #

46
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:27,480
# but I'll be there for you #

47
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:29,310
# When the rain starts to pour #

48
00:02:29,310 --> 00:02:32,430
# I'll be there for you #

49
00:02:32,430 --> 00:02:34,270
# Like I've been there before #

50
00:02:34,270 --> 00:02:37,280
# I'll be there for you #

51
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:40,940
# 'Cause you're there for me too #

52
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:51,000
- Here you go. You can wear this.     - Thanks.

53
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:53,000
Okay.

54
00:02:55,250 --> 00:02:57,630
Oh, I'm setting the phone down.

55
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:00,220
But I'm still here.

56
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:03,340
Just don't go anywhere. I'm still here.

57
00:03:03,510 --> 00:03:07,600
Don't switch or anything, because I'm right here. Just one sec.

58
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:11,560
One sec. One second.

59
00:03:11,730 --> 00:03:14,400
- Wait. One second. Just...     - Phoebe?

60
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:16,900
What? Monica, I'm scared.

61
00:03:17,360 --> 00:03:20,990
Okay. Honey, that's a sleeve, okay?

62
00:03:21,150 --> 00:03:23,700
And we also have speakerphone.

63
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:25,700
Please stay on the line.

64
00:03:25,870 --> 00:03:27,200
Your call is important to us.

65
00:03:27,370 --> 00:03:29,410
You gotta hang up. Because we're gonna be late.

66
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:32,460
Thank you for your patience. You're the next caller.

67
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:35,290
Yes. Yes. I'm the next caller.

68
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:37,840
You were gonna have me hang up.

69
00:03:39,670 --> 00:03:40,960
Hey.

70
00:03:41,510 --> 00:03:43,840
Can you take a duck and a chick to the theater?

71
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:46,510
- Of course not.     - No.

72
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:49,770
Okay, I just wanted them to hear it from somebody else.

73
00:03:54,270 --> 00:03:55,310

74
00:03:57,270 --> 00:03:59,900
- Hey. Hey, Rach. Hi.     - Oh, hi, how are you?

75
00:04:00,070 --> 00:04:02,530
- Good.     - Hey. Ha, ha.

76
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:06,160
- Ahem. Looks like we're the first ones here.     - Yeah, looks that way.

77
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:07,530
First ones here.

78
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:13,210
Hmm. Oh, Tommy, this is Ross. Ross, Tommy.

79
00:04:13,370 --> 00:04:16,000
- Hey.     - Oh, I'm sorry. This is Cailin. Cailin...

80
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:17,790
Sorry.

81
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:19,750
And break.

82
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:25,510
Okay, uh, I think I'm gonna run to the ladies' room.

83
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:28,430
- Okay. I'll get our seats.     - I'll join you.

84
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:32,350
So, uh... Well, this is, uh...

85
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:33,850
This is awkward.

86
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:35,190
Yeah?

87
00:04:35,350 --> 00:04:38,150
Well, you know, because Rachel and I used to go out. Ha, ha.

88
00:04:38,310 --> 00:04:39,940
Oh, I didn't know that.

89
00:04:42,190 --> 00:04:44,990
Well, then this is awkward.

90
00:04:46,570 --> 00:04:49,700
- So, what do you? Oh. Yeah.     - I think we're here. Yeah.

91
00:04:51,490 --> 00:04:53,290
Excuse me. I'm sorry.

92
00:04:53,450 --> 00:04:55,870
I think you may be in our seats.

93
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:59,250
Um, no, I don't think so.

94
00:04:59,420 --> 00:05:02,250
- Could we take a look at your ticket?     - Sure.

95
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:06,720
Yeah. Yeah, see, this says, "D-13."

96
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:09,510
- And...     - Oh, well, I thought that...

97
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:13,970
You thought, huh? Yeah, well, that didn't really work out too well for you. Idiot!

98
00:05:15,060 --> 00:05:18,600
What are you, a moron? Huh? It says, "D-13." Okay?

99
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:21,980
Look, you're surrounded by even numbers. Does that give you some clue?

100
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:25,400
- Well, the usher told me...     - Oh. Oh, the usher must be right.

101
00:05:25,570 --> 00:05:29,240
What, with all his training they go through. Get out!

102
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:31,200
Here.

103
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:37,250
- Hey, man, you want the aisle?     - No, I'm good.

104
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:45,000

105
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:51,260
- There he is.     - There's our star.

106
00:05:51,430 --> 00:05:53,010
You were great.

107
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:54,510
So? So? What'd you think?

108
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:58,640
Almost as good as the play with the two naked girls on the seesaw.

109
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:01,650
- I wasn't in that.     - I know.

110
00:06:02,570 --> 00:06:05,900
Hey, Kate, listen I want you to meet everybody. Everybody, this is Kate.

111
00:06:06,070 --> 00:06:09,200
- Excuse me. Excuse me. Sweetheart.     - Hi.

112
00:06:11,410 --> 00:06:12,740
Come.

113
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:18,460
So that's the girl you like.

114
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:23,380
I'm telling you, this guy Rachel is with is crazy, okay?

115
00:06:23,540 --> 00:06:26,250
He viciously screamed at total strangers.

116
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:28,720
I think he's bad news.

117
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:33,680
Wait a minute, wait a minute. You don't like the guy Rachel's dating?

118
00:06:33,850 --> 00:06:35,010
Well, that's odd.

119
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:39,770
Oh, hey, Lauren. Uh, you guys, this is Kate's understudy, Lauren.

120
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:42,940
- Hi.     - Hey, gosh, you look so familiar.

121
00:06:43,110 --> 00:06:45,980
Oh, yeah. I ran into you in the hallway in your building.

122
00:06:46,150 --> 00:06:50,200
It was right after I slept with Joey. He dumped me the next day.

123
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:53,660
So how'd you guys meet?

124
00:06:54,530 --> 00:06:58,120
Well, uh, the short version is, I pursued her for a couple of months.

125
00:06:58,290 --> 00:07:01,290
Then I gave her a check for $20,000 and she was mine.

126
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:07,460
Yeah, and in the long version, I dump him for telling people the short version.

127
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:11,220
Joey, sweetheart, you were fabulous.

128
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:14,510
Hey, you guys, this is my agent, Estelle.

129
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:15,890
How do you do?

130
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:19,520
Oh, you two girls were outstanding.

131
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:21,980
Do they have representation?

132
00:07:22,690 --> 00:07:24,520
They weren't in the play.

133
00:07:24,690 --> 00:07:27,400
- Huh. We're not actors.     - Oh. What a shame.

134
00:07:27,570 --> 00:07:30,030
Because with her face and her chest...

135
00:07:30,190 --> 00:07:31,950
...I could really put something together.

136
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:36,160
Could I borrow it?

137
00:07:37,990 --> 00:07:40,450
Hi. Remember me?

138
00:07:40,620 --> 00:07:43,500
Hi. Yeah. Ahem, Tommy's in line for the bathroom...

139
00:07:43,670 --> 00:07:46,630
...and someone just cut in front of him. I think he's gonna snap.

140
00:07:48,130 --> 00:07:51,170
- Ross, I'm gonna go.     - Go? Why?

141
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:53,880
I don't know. Could be because I don't feel like...

142
00:07:54,050 --> 00:07:57,470
...standing around all night, waiting for some guy who may or may not scream.

143
00:07:57,640 --> 00:08:00,060
Oh, but Cailin...

144
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:02,230
...he definitely will scream.

145
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:04,520
Goodbye, Ross.

146
00:08:04,690 --> 00:08:06,730
Oh, go, all right.

147
00:08:08,820 --> 00:08:11,110
Here we go, people.

148
00:08:15,950 --> 00:08:19,280
Ahem, "Boxing Day.

149
00:08:19,450 --> 00:08:21,410
The Lucille Lortel Theatre..."

150
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:28,540
"Joey Tribbiani gives an uneven performance.

151
00:08:28,710 --> 00:08:31,960
But Mr. Tribbiani is not the worst thing in this production."

152
00:08:32,130 --> 00:08:34,420
Yes. Ha-ha-ha!

153
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:41,220
"Kate Miller's awkward and mannered portrayal is laughable."

154
00:08:42,890 --> 00:08:44,810
Here it is. "The direction...

155
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:48,270
...by Marshall Townend is..."

156
00:08:54,530 --> 00:08:56,570
Thank you, boys and girls.

157
00:08:56,740 --> 00:08:59,120
You've ruined my life.

158
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:02,740
Please stuff your talentless faces...

159
00:09:02,910 --> 00:09:06,250
...with my mother's crab cakes.

160
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:08,250
Excuse me.

161
00:09:13,510 --> 00:09:15,840
Does anyone mind if I save this?

162
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:20,760
- Hey.     - Hey.

163
00:09:20,930 --> 00:09:22,850
- Oh, is the play over?     - Yeah, where were you?

164
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:25,060
Thank you for your patience.

165
00:09:25,230 --> 00:09:27,190
You're the next caller.

166
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:31,020
You were the next caller five hours ago. You must be going crazy.

167
00:09:31,190 --> 00:09:34,110
No, I've kept myself busy.

168
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:45,040
Oh, okay, yeah, I put your stuff in her room and her stuff in your room.

169
00:09:50,380 --> 00:09:51,880
Hey.

170
00:09:52,170 --> 00:09:53,170
You okay?

171
00:09:54,510 --> 00:09:55,510
Fabulous.

172
00:09:55,880 --> 00:10:00,760
Listen, drama critics, they're nothing but people who couldn't make it as actors.

173
00:10:00,930 --> 00:10:03,220
- You know what you should do?     - Become a drama critic.

174
00:10:08,140 --> 00:10:10,230
I am hurt.

175
00:10:12,520 --> 00:10:14,190
A plague...

176
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:17,190
...on both your houses.

177
00:10:19,070 --> 00:10:22,740
By the way, he dumped me tonight after he read my review.

178
00:10:22,910 --> 00:10:24,700
Oh, classy.

179
00:10:25,290 --> 00:10:26,790
Yep.

180
00:10:26,950 --> 00:10:29,250
I sure know how to pick them, huh?

181
00:10:30,420 --> 00:10:32,580
You know I gave up a part on a soap for this?

182
00:10:34,670 --> 00:10:37,710
Yeah, I, uh... I gave up a job too.

183
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:40,760
- Really? What?     - Uh, declawing cats.

184
00:10:42,760 --> 00:10:45,560
Hey, tell you what, let me walk you home.

185
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:49,930
We'll stop by every newsstand and burn every copy of their Times and The Post.

186
00:10:50,140 --> 00:10:52,520
- Why The Post?     - You didn't see The Post?

187
00:10:52,690 --> 00:10:55,610
- No. You?     - No. Why?

188
00:11:02,910 --> 00:11:05,990
You really think these newspapers are just jealous of me?

189
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:09,370
Oh, absolutely. You're talented and you're good-looking.

190
00:11:09,830 --> 00:11:12,460
Aw, you're sweet and cute.

191
00:11:12,630 --> 00:11:15,040
I know. That's why they trashed me.

192
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:24,470
- Wait. Wait a minute.     - What?

193
00:11:26,350 --> 00:11:28,180
I don't get you.

194
00:11:28,350 --> 00:11:30,430
I mean, first you hate me.

195
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:33,560
Then you sleep with me.

196
00:11:33,730 --> 00:11:36,650
Then you want nothing to do with me. Now you want me again?

197
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:39,440
What? So you never went out with an actress before?

198
00:11:40,860 --> 00:11:43,660
Kate, do you even like me?

199
00:11:46,450 --> 00:11:50,160
- Of course I do.     - So how come you blew me off?

200
00:11:50,330 --> 00:11:53,960
- You know, how come you were with him?     - I don't know.

201
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:56,500
I just do this.

202
00:11:56,670 --> 00:11:59,550
I always have to pick, like, the smartest guy...

203
00:11:59,710 --> 00:12:02,300
...or the most talented guy.

204
00:12:03,050 --> 00:12:05,390
Why can't I just pick someone like you?

205
00:12:08,470 --> 00:12:09,970
Thanks.

206
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:13,890
You know what I mean.

207
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:17,940
I mean, like, the sweetest guy.

208
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:20,650
Joey, you're just so...

209
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:24,070
You're so...

210
00:12:24,860 --> 00:12:26,240
...so...

211
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:36,830
Okay. Okay, okay. Ha, ha.

212
00:12:37,670 --> 00:12:41,000
Here we go. Let's get your feet up there.

213
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:49,890
Good night, Kate.

214
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:52,470
Sweet dreams.

215
00:12:58,940 --> 00:13:02,480
I'm gonna put this can right here in case you have to hurl.

216
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,910
Please stay on the line.

217
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:15,210
Your call is very important to us.

218
00:13:16,290 --> 00:13:19,790
Pheebs, you've been up for 24 hours. Go to sleep, honey.

219
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:22,960
- This isn't healthy.     - No, no, I'm fine.

220
00:13:23,130 --> 00:13:26,630
And you know why? Because of all the riboflavin.

221
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:31,050
- Hey.     - Hey.

222
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:34,060
Didn't you have that outfit on last night?

223
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:36,850
Yeah. I stayed at Kate's, but, uh, nothing happened.

224
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:39,650
Hey, Pheebs, where were you?

225
00:13:39,810 --> 00:13:43,570
I'm so, so sorry, Joey. I am definitely gonna see your play.

226
00:13:43,730 --> 00:13:47,360
I swear, your play is very important to us. Thank you for your patience.

227
00:13:47,530 --> 00:13:50,320
Your play is the next play I'm gonna see.

228
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:54,660
- Anyway, how'd it go with Kate?     - Oh, it was great.

229
00:13:54,830 --> 00:13:56,250
Yeah, I walked her home...

230
00:13:56,410 --> 00:13:59,710
...and it was amazing how much we connected, you know?

231
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:01,420
Then she passed out.

232
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:03,290
But then she woke up. Yeah.

233
00:14:03,460 --> 00:14:05,380
And we stayed up all night talking.

234
00:14:05,550 --> 00:14:08,260
And now we're, like, totally crazy about each other.

235
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:12,350
- Joey, you had "the night."     - What?

236
00:14:12,510 --> 00:14:15,270
When two people finally realize their feelings for each other...

237
00:14:15,430 --> 00:14:19,270
...and they talk for hours and they learn all about the other person.

238
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,480
You think?

239
00:14:20,650 --> 00:14:23,610
- Ha, ha. Did you learn about her family?     - Two brothers. One died.

240
00:14:23,770 --> 00:14:25,610
- Yes.     - Yeah.

241
00:14:32,070 --> 00:14:33,990
This is from the woman at the bar.

242
00:14:38,790 --> 00:14:41,540
Sorry. She thought you were somebody else.

243
00:14:45,170 --> 00:14:46,920
- What time is it?     - One.

244
00:14:47,090 --> 00:14:48,670
Seven-fifteen.

245
00:14:49,340 --> 00:14:50,720
Watch doesn't work.

246
00:14:52,090 --> 00:14:55,310
Tommy's supposed to be here soon. We're going to lunch.

247
00:14:57,810 --> 00:15:01,690
Look. Look, I wasn't gonna say anything to you, but...

248
00:15:01,850 --> 00:15:05,520
All right, I don't think you should be seeing Tommy anymore.

249
00:15:06,650 --> 00:15:07,860
- You don't?     - No.

250
00:15:08,030 --> 00:15:12,450
The guy is mean. I mean, really mean. I think you should stay away from him.

251
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:16,990
Hmm. Or maybe I should stay away from all men.

252
00:15:17,410 --> 00:15:19,660
No, it's not just because I'm jealous.

253
00:15:21,330 --> 00:15:24,250
I mean, I'm not, I'm not. I'm not jealous, okay?

254
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:25,960
Look, the guy, he screamed...

255
00:15:26,130 --> 00:15:29,010
...he actually screamed at this couple sitting in our seats.

256
00:15:29,170 --> 00:15:31,840
Yeah, and at the end of the play, he...

257
00:15:32,010 --> 00:15:36,800
He got up, you know, and he just started, like, banging his hands together.

258
00:15:39,270 --> 00:15:42,020
Okay, fine. Fine. You don't want to believe me, no, that's fine.

259
00:15:42,190 --> 00:15:44,940
- We're kidding. Ross.     - Ross. Ross.

260
00:15:46,070 --> 00:15:48,980
No one believe me. I'm Mr. Funny to you. Mr. Funny.

261
00:15:49,150 --> 00:15:50,190
Sorry, Tommy.

262
00:15:50,860 --> 00:15:52,360
What's in the cup, Ross?

263
00:15:53,530 --> 00:15:56,200
- Um.     - What is in the cup?

264
00:15:56,370 --> 00:15:57,530
Okay, it's coffee.

265
00:15:57,700 --> 00:16:00,040
Iced coffee? Tell me it's iced coffee.

266
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:04,710
- It's hot...     - Hot coffee!

267
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:08,500
You idiot! You gonna spill hot coffee all over me, huh?

268
00:16:08,670 --> 00:16:12,420
What are you? Just a big, stupid doofy idiot with a doofy idiot hairdo?

269
00:16:17,550 --> 00:16:19,810
What's your favorite thing about summertime?

270
00:16:19,970 --> 00:16:23,890
Hmm, going to the beach when it stays light real late.

271
00:16:24,060 --> 00:16:25,400
Yeah.

272
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:29,020
- Hey.     - Tommy.

273
00:16:29,190 --> 00:16:31,360
Say, what's your favorite thing about summer?

274
00:16:31,530 --> 00:16:35,530
Ooh, I don't know. Probably the, uh, smell of freshly cut grass.

275
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:37,570
- Aw, that's a good one.     - Yeah.

276
00:16:42,410 --> 00:16:46,500
Hey, sorry. Sorry I'm late. My duck and my chick had a fight. It was ugly.

277
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:49,380
- Look, we held the curtain for you. Let's go.     - Okay.

278
00:16:54,840 --> 00:16:58,430
Vic. Where have you been, baby?

279
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:04,730
- Where's Kate?     - She got a job in L.A.

280
00:17:05,730 --> 00:17:07,060
What?

281
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:12,440
I've been waiting up all night for you. Where have you been?

282
00:17:13,360 --> 00:17:15,780
Where have you been, Vic?

283
00:17:16,610 --> 00:17:18,280
Oh, uh... Go to the window.

284
00:17:18,450 --> 00:17:21,660
I wanna run down to the truck and show you something.

285
00:17:24,040 --> 00:17:26,460
What do you got down there, Vic?

286
00:17:26,620 --> 00:17:28,420
What do you got under that tarp?

287
00:17:32,340 --> 00:17:33,420
When is she leaving?

288
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:36,340
Tonight. What are you doing?

289
00:17:38,010 --> 00:17:39,800
I'm coming up.

290
00:17:42,640 --> 00:17:44,470
Hey, you mind if I use the phone?

291
00:17:50,150 --> 00:17:52,860
Why don't you use ours across the hall because she...

292
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,440
...has problems.

293
00:17:54,610 --> 00:17:55,940
Thanks.

294
00:17:58,820 --> 00:18:02,740
Sorry, Tommy. I almost spilled this hot coffee on you.

295
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:05,660
Ha, ha. Yeah, but you didn't. Ha, ha.

296
00:18:05,830 --> 00:18:08,660
No, but it's hot.

297
00:18:12,630 --> 00:18:15,130
Ross, would you just stop it? It's getting really old.

298
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:17,340
I can't believe no one believes me.

299
00:18:17,670 --> 00:18:19,090
I do. I believe you.

300
00:18:19,550 --> 00:18:20,640
You do, Pheebs?

301
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:24,180
Yeah. But I also believed her when she said I was next.

302
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:31,850
Ooh, hey.

303
00:18:32,230 --> 00:18:33,820
Hey there, little fella.

304
00:18:33,980 --> 00:18:36,360
Mr. Fuzzy-Man, how you doing?

305
00:18:40,530 --> 00:18:42,200
Gross.

306
00:18:42,370 --> 00:18:44,120
Idiot!

307
00:18:44,280 --> 00:18:47,330
Stupid, little, fuzzy, yellow creature!

308
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:51,460
"Oh, look at me. I'm so cute. I'm a little chick who's disgusting!"

309
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:54,130
God, you're so stupid! How are you not yet extinct?

310
00:18:57,380 --> 00:18:59,300
What are you quacking about?

311
00:18:59,470 --> 00:19:01,050
Dumb Donald Dodo!

312
00:19:05,260 --> 00:19:07,890
Step away from the duck.

313
00:19:11,060 --> 00:19:13,190
Ooh, sorry, little Mr. Chickadee.

314
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:15,730
Sorry you went doody in my hand!

315
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:20,570
Well, I guess we're not going out anymore.

316
00:19:20,740 --> 00:19:22,110
Man!

317
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:27,740
- Joey.     - Kate.

318
00:19:27,910 --> 00:19:29,950
I'm so glad I caught you. I couldn't find you before.

319
00:19:30,120 --> 00:19:32,330
What's going on? What's all this about L. A?

320
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:34,580
They still want me for General Hospital.

321
00:19:34,790 --> 00:19:37,550
But what about us?

322
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:41,670
Last night was wonderful.

323
00:19:42,090 --> 00:19:44,090
But I can't stay here just for you.

324
00:19:44,340 --> 00:19:47,100
Well, so stay for the museums.

325
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:50,350
- I'm sorry.     - Joey, on-stage.

326
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:53,270
Well, can you stay till the end of the play?

327
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:56,270
I mean, I'll go to the airport with you. I want to say goodbye.

328
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:58,360
Where are you, Vic?

329
00:19:58,530 --> 00:20:00,690
Flight's in an hour. I gotta go.

330
00:20:00,860 --> 00:20:02,320
Vic?

331
00:20:02,490 --> 00:20:03,910
Vic?

332
00:20:05,450 --> 00:20:07,450
- Vic!     - In a minute.

333
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:11,950
So this is it, Victor?

334
00:20:12,790 --> 00:20:15,750
Yeah. I guess it is.

335
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:24,630
Listen, I, uh...

336
00:20:24,930 --> 00:20:28,640
I gotta say goodbye, and I gotta say it quick because this is killing me.

337
00:20:29,310 --> 00:20:33,890
One thing you gotta know is that I will never forget you.

338
00:20:34,140 --> 00:20:37,360
But you got things you have to do now.

339
00:20:37,520 --> 00:20:39,320
And so do I.

340
00:20:40,980 --> 00:20:42,530
And so...

341
00:20:44,490 --> 00:20:46,950
...I'm gonna get on this spaceship...

342
00:20:54,330 --> 00:20:57,790
...and I'm gonna go to Blaargon-7 in search of alternative fuels.

343
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:03,170
But when I return 200 years from now...

344
00:21:03,340 --> 00:21:05,470
...you'll be long gone...

345
00:21:06,090 --> 00:21:08,550
...but I won't have aged at all.

346
00:21:11,850 --> 00:21:15,560
So you tell your great, great granddaughter...

347
00:21:15,730 --> 00:21:16,890
...to look me up.

348
00:21:19,020 --> 00:21:21,070
Because, Adrianne...

349
00:21:21,230 --> 00:21:22,780
...baby...

350
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:26,530
...I'm gonna want to meet her.

351
00:21:34,290 --> 00:21:36,580
So long, Vic.

352
00:21:43,380 --> 00:21:46,340
Phoebe, it's been two days.

353
00:21:46,510 --> 00:21:48,050
Yeah, I know.

354
00:21:48,220 --> 00:21:51,220
Ugh, good thing it's one of those 801 numbers, right?

355
00:21:51,390 --> 00:21:56,480
Phoebe, 800 is toll free. 801 is Utah.

356
00:21:59,060 --> 00:22:00,190
No, no, no.

357
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:03,860
It has to be 800 because all those big companies have 800 numbers.

358
00:22:04,030 --> 00:22:05,400
Every...

359
00:22:05,740 --> 00:22:09,200
Yeah, every big Utah-based company has one.

360
00:22:09,570 --> 00:22:10,570
Phoebe.

361
00:22:10,740 --> 00:22:13,830
Sorry. I'm so sorry. I will pay you back.

362
00:22:13,990 --> 00:22:16,830
And yet she's still not hanging up the phone.

363
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:18,710
- Hang up.     - Hang up the phone.

364
00:22:18,870 --> 00:22:20,420
Fine. Fine.

365
00:22:25,090 --> 00:22:26,510
What?

366
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:30,340
Well, I think I broke it.

367
00:22:32,260 --> 00:22:34,600
But that's all right. Here's the number where you can call.

